<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Koskari -- a Lisp that lives with Python</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Koskari is a Lisp that runs on its own stackless evaluator inside CPython. It awaits without async markers, reads indentation as layout, and takes Python modules, classes, and objects both ways.">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Koskari">
  <meta property="og:description" content="A Lisp that lives with Python. First-class continuations, ambient async, indentation layout.">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,700&family=Hanken+Grotesk:wght@400;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="koskari-icon.svg">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>

<body>
<div class="ko-page">

  <nav class="ko-nav">
    <div class="ko-brand">
      <img src="koskari-icon.svg" alt="" width="34" height="34">
      <span class="ko-brand-name">Koskari</span>
      <span class="ko-version">v{{ version }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ko-nav-links">
      <a class="ko-link" href="/docs/">Docs</a>
      <a class="ko-link" href="#examples">Examples</a>
      <a class="ko-link" href="#install">Install</a>
      <a class="ko-link" href="{{ github_url }}">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main>

  <section class="ko-opening">
    <div>
      <h1 class="ko-h1">A Lisp that lives<br><span class="ko-accent">with Python.</span></h1>
      <p class="ko-lede">Koskari is a Lisp that runs on its own <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/reference/vm/">stackless evaluator inside CPython</a>. It <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/guide/demand-async-and-defer/">awaits without async markers</a>, reads <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/guide/layout-and-s-expressions/">indentation as layout</a>, and takes <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/tutorials/from-python/interop/">Python modules, classes, and objects both ways</a>, <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/tutorials/from-python/classes-and-objects/">subclassing</a> included.</p>
      <div class="ko-cta-row">
        <a class="ko-btn ko-btn-primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Quickstart</a>
        <a class="ko-btn ko-btn-secondary" href="/docs/tutorials/beginner/">Little Koskari</a>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-install">
        <span class="ko-install-cmd"><span class="ko-prompt">$</span> pip install "koskari[repl]"</span>
        <span class="ko-install-soon">v{{ version }} BETA</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="ko-code-window ko-code-opening">
        <div class="ko-code-chrome">
          <span class="ko-code-filename">{{ samples.move_ki.filename }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ko-code-body"><pre class="ko-code-pre">{{ samples.move_ki.code }}</pre></div>
      </div>
      <p class="ko-compare-caption">The <span class="ko-inline-code">&amp;</span> formals receive <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/guide/bindings-and-refs/">references</a>, so one function updates a dict item, a list index, or an attribute in place.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="beside" class="ko-section ko-section-tight">
    <h2 class="ko-label ko-label-tight">Python beside Koskari</h2>
    <div class="ko-compare">
      <div class="ko-code-window">
        <div class="ko-code-chrome">
          <span class="ko-code-filename">{{ samples.shapes_py.filename }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ko-code-body"><pre class="ko-code-pre">{{ samples.shapes_py.code }}</pre></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-code-window">
        <div class="ko-code-chrome">
          <span class="ko-code-filename">{{ samples.shapes_ki.filename }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ko-code-body"><pre class="ko-code-pre">{{ samples.shapes_ki.code }}</pre></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ko-compare-caption">Python's <span class="ko-inline-code">=</span> splits into <span class="ko-inline-code">define</span> for a new name and <span class="ko-inline-code">set!</span> for one that exists, and a parameter list is written in brackets. <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/tutorials/from-python/map/">The map from Python</a> covers imports, attributes, control flow, and literals.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="examples" class="ko-section ko-section-tight">
    <h2 class="ko-label ko-label-tight">Three examples</h2>

    <h3 class="ko-section-title">Async without the marker</h3>
    <p class="ko-section-lede">Nothing in this program is marked async. Awaitable values are awaited where they are used, <span class="ko-inline-code">defer</span> holds a call for <span class="ko-inline-code">gather</span>, and every function is already an ordinary <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/guide/demand-async-and-defer/">coroutine</a>.</p>
    <div class="ko-code-window">
      <div class="ko-code-chrome">
        <span class="ko-code-filename">{{ samples.fetch_ki.filename }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-code-body"><pre class="ko-code-pre">{{ samples.fetch_ki.code }}</pre></div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="ko-section-title ko-section-title-spaced">A macro that retries</h3>
    <p class="ko-section-lede"><span class="ko-inline-code">retry</span> is a <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/guide/macros-and-hygiene/">macro</a>, so its body waits until the expansion asks for it. The template is written in the same layout as the code calling it, and its loop is a <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/guide/model-of-evaluation/">tail call</a>.</p>
    <div class="ko-code-window">
      <div class="ko-code-chrome">
        <span class="ko-code-filename">{{ samples.retry_ki.filename }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-code-body"><pre class="ko-code-pre">{{ samples.retry_ki.code }}</pre></div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="ko-section-title ko-section-title-spaced">A search, with no search engine</h3>
    <p class="ko-section-lede"><span class="ko-inline-code">amb</span> is an ordinary function. Each call captures the rest of the search as a <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/reference/runtime/koskari-solve/">delimited continuation</a> and runs it once per choice; <span class="ko-inline-code">require</span> abandons the branches that cannot work.</p>
    <div class="ko-code-window">
      <div class="ko-code-chrome">
        <span class="ko-code-filename">{{ samples.triples_ki.filename }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-code-body"><pre class="ko-code-pre">{{ samples.triples_ki.code }}</pre></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ko-section ko-section-tight">
    <h2 class="ko-label ko-label-tight">Documentation</h2>
    <p class="ko-doc-line"><a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/quickstart/">Quickstart</a> &middot; <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/tutorials/beginner/">Little Koskari</a> &middot; <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/tutorials/from-python/">From Python</a> &middot; <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/guide/">Guide</a> &middot; <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/reference/">Reference</a> &middot; <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/reference/api/">Python API</a> &middot; <a class="ko-text-link" href="/docs/faq/">FAQ</a></p>
  </section>

  <section id="install" class="ko-download">
    <div class="ko-download-grid">
      <div>
        <h2 class="ko-download-title">Get Koskari</h2>
        <p class="ko-download-lede">Koskari <strong class="ko-download-strong">v{{ version }}</strong> is the first beta, so <a class="ko-ink-link" href="/docs/project/release-and-versioning/">expect the language surface to move</a> before 1.0. It installs from PyPI and <a class="ko-ink-link" href="/docs/faq/#which-python-versions-and-platforms">runs on CPython 3.9 through 3.14 on Linux and macOS</a>. It is <a class="ko-ink-link" href="/docs/faq/#what-is-it-not">not a replacement for Python</a>. A Python program can also <a class="ko-ink-link" href="/docs/guide/hosting-from-python/">embed it</a>.</p>
        <div class="ko-platform-tags">
          <span class="ko-platform-tag">Linux</span>
          <span class="ko-platform-tag">macOS</span>
          <span class="ko-platform-tag">CPython 3.9-3.14</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-download-cmds">
        <div class="ko-cmd-box">
          <div class="ko-cmd-label">PyPI</div>
          <div class="ko-cmd-line"><span class="ko-cmd-prompt">$</span> pip install "koskari[repl]"</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ko-cmd-box">
          <div class="ko-cmd-label">From source</div>
          <div class="ko-cmd-line"><span class="ko-cmd-prompt">$</span> git clone {{ repo_short }}</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  </main>

  <footer class="ko-footer">
    <div class="ko-footer-brand">
      <img src="koskari-icon.svg" alt="" width="26" height="26">
      <span class="ko-footer-name">Koskari</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ko-footer-meta">{{ license_label }} &middot; <span class="ko-footer-end"># The end.</span></div>
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
